# Component lab (`/dev`)

The lab is optional and isolated. Routes: `src/app/dev`. Internals: `src/dev` (English copy, meta, chrome, playgrounds, galleries). Product code must not import either folder. Deleting both (or leaving them in `.dockerignore`) removes `/dev` from the build. Proxy skips `/dev` as a routing exemption only.

It is not the product site. Entry is a manual URL (`/dev`, `/dev/test`, `/dev/tokens`, `/dev/components/[slug]`, `/dev/templates/[slug]`, `/dev/icons`). English only. Playground LTR/RTL (preview Card `dir` only); no dark mode; no locale routing. Lab copy lives in `src/dev/copy.ts`, not product dictionaries. The lab shell uses `Container width="full"`.

In the **same turn** as any change to UI, Templates, Icons, theme tokens (`src/settings`, `globals.css`), or component config, update the lab so docs, playgrounds, and galleries stay complete:

- New/changed UI or template → `src/dev/meta/<name>.ts` (register in `index.ts`), playground renderer in `src/dev/playground/renderers.tsx`, permutation gallery in `src/dev/gallery`
- Tokens → `/dev/tokens` (`src/dev/tokens.tsx`)
- Icons / registry → `/dev/icons`

Do not finish a component or token change while `/dev` is stale. Do not put lab chrome in `SiteHeader` or dictionaries.
